## Workflow Board

A kanban whose columns are a Workflow card's states, in the Workflow's own order, built on the catalog Board.

```gts
<WorkflowBoard
  @workflow={{@model.workflow}}
  @cards={{this.boardCards}}
  @onMove={{this.runWorkflow}}
  @onOpen={{this.open}}
/>
```

- **Moves go through the caller.** `onMove(card, toStateKey, note)` resolves to accept and rejects with a reason to refuse; the board shows that reason, and the card stays where its data says it is.
- **Guarded moves ask first.** A transition whose guard is `requires-note` opens an inline prompt, and only a confirmed note commits the move.
- **Headers carry risk.** Each column header shows the nearest breach among its cards, so the board doubles as a risk view.

The linked example shows the support case workflow over five cases. Moves are refused there, since an example never edits the cards it shows.

### Non-goals

It runs no workflow logic of its own: the caller decides what a move does.
